# Public origin of the deployed site. Used for canonical URLs, Open Graph
# metadata, robots.txt and the sitemap. The production build REFUSES to run
# without it, because the value is baked in at build time and cannot be
# corrected at runtime.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://example.com

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Quotation form delivery — REQUIRED before launch.
#
# `src/app/api/quote/route.ts` returns 503 with neither of the options below
# configured, and the form then shows its error state. That is deliberate: a
# visitor told the message failed can phone instead, whereas one told it
# succeeded cannot. Do not go live without setting one of these.
#
# Option 1 — e-mail via Resend (https://resend.com). The from address must be
# on a domain verified in the Resend dashboard; the to address is wherever the
# enquiries should land. Replies go to the buyer, not to the site.
# RESEND_API_KEY=re_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
# QUOTE_TO_EMAIL=teklif@raymarnuts.com
# QUOTE_FROM_EMAIL=site@raymarnuts.com

# Option 2 — POST the enquiry as JSON to a CRM, Zapier, Make, n8n or any other
# endpoint that accepts it. Checked only when the Resend variables are absent.
# QUOTE_WEBHOOK_URL=https://hooks.example.com/raymar-quote

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local only. Suppresses the two HTTPS-forcing headers so a production build
# can be opened over plain HTTP on the LAN — e.g. from a phone at
# http://<mac-ip>:3100. Headers are resolved into the routes manifest at BUILD
# time, so this belongs on `next build`, not on `next start`.
#
# NEVER set this in production: it disables HSTS and upgrade-insecure-requests.
# ALLOW_INSECURE_LAN=1
